{"number": 45, "text": "                    Exercises\n\n\n           19.1\n                    Look at the phrasal verbs in A, Then match the questions 1-6 with the appropriate answers a-f\n                    below.\n                    1 These  shoes are a bit expensive - do you think | should buy them?\n                    2  Ohdear, look at that accident.\n                    3 What  did you think of the restaurant?\n                    4  Do you know what CV means?\n                    5 Would  you like to go to a café?\n                    6 Who  are you supporting in the league?\n                    a) Couldn’t have asked for anything better!\n                    b) Yes, go for it!\n                    c) Quick! Send for an ambulance!\n                    d) Yes, I’m dying for an ice cream.\n                    e) We’re rooting for the Reds, as usual.\n                    f) Sure! It stands for curriculum vitae.\n            19.2\n                    Complete  these sentences with an appropriate verb. Write the verb in the correct form.\n                       He                 for a doctor as soon as he felt the pains in his chest.\n\n                       Martha                 for her work, so she’s going to find it very hard when she has to retire.\n                       These boots don’t really               with this skirt, but they’re comfortable.\n                       You                 for a nicer teacher. She’s so patient and kind.\n                          have to have a word with Gina. | can’t             up with her rudeness any longer!\n                       Your hair is too long - you             with a haircut.\n                       You should                 with the course. it would be a shame to give up now.\n                       | love going back to my home town and                up with all my old friends.\n            19.3\n                    Use  a phrasal verb from the opposite page to complete these dialogues.\n                     1   Anna      This fish tastes delicious with your tomato sauce.\n                         Isabelle  Yes, they do               well                each other, don’t they!\n                    2    Charles   Shall we go to the concert together?\n                                   Good idea. I'll              you on the way there. |\n                    3.             I’ve bought two bottles of water. |\n                         Elliot    Great, I’m               something to drink.\n                    4    Fran      | thought the film was great.\n                         Millie    Yes, | thought it             the theme of love really sensitively.\n                    5\n                         Michael   Let’s meet for a coffee and a chat next week.\n\n                        Darcy      Yes, | CaN’t  CO\n\n                    Rewrite  these sentences using phrasal verbs from the opposite page.\n            19.4\n                       |        tolerate such noisy neighbours as yours.\n\n                       It’s been such a busy week. | can’t wait for the weekend.\n                       Evelyn's shoes match her handbag perfectly.\n                       All the students at his university were hoping Austin would win the golf championship.\n                       | have the best job you could imagine.\n                       Her grandson is the most important person in Stella’s life.\n\n\n                                                                   English Phrasal Verbs in Use Intermediate\n                                                                                                               43", "char_count": 3572, "mean_conf": 91.25, "word_count": 420, "words": [{"text": "19.1", "x0": 239, "y0": 360, "x1": 343, "y1": 398, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "19.2", "x0": 244, "y0": 1210, "x1": 350, "y1": 1250, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "19.3", "x0": 250, "y0": 1756, "x1": 356, "y1": 1794, "conf": 95, "bold": true}, {"text":